# Intent: The pairing key and the hub's private address are entered on the Wi-Fi setup page (patches P01 to P05), never in an image. Two optional fields, three strings (English and Spanish). The page checks the shape of both before it joins Wi-Fi, saves them only after Wi-Fi joined, and zeroes its copy of the key. A unit built without the client refuses the two fields when they are filled in.
# Placement: unit (the setup page is the unit's own and works with the host off)
# Upstream: firmware/portal/ of this tree, which replaces the access point source of the 78__esp-wifi-connect component (MIT)
# Check after a flash: the setup page shows 'Travel key (optional)' and 'Home hub's private address (optional)'; a key that does not start with tskey- is refused with a plain sentence and nothing is saved; a good key and address are saved after the Wi-Fi joins (self.tailnet.status says key_saved and peer_saved).
# Kconfig: MAIPAI_WIFI_PORTAL (the page); the fields work with MAIPAI_TAILNET.
diff --git a/firmware/portal/maipai_portal_core.h b/firmware/portal/maipai_portal_core.h
